.TH TERMNAV-NAVIGATE 1 "2026-08-25" "termnav" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
termnav-navigate \- route pane and tab navigation through nested terminal scopes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B termnav-navigate
.I ACTION DIRECTION
.PP
.B termnav-navigate
.B --parent
.I ACTION DIRECTION
.B --client-pid
.I PID
.B --client-tty
.I TTY
.B --client-created
.I SECONDS
.B --client-termtype
.I TYPE
.B --source-socket
.I PATH
.B --source-pane
.I PANE
.RI [ --source-session " SESSION" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B termnav-navigate
routes one semantic navigation request through application, tmux, SSH relay,
and terminal scopes. It visits local tmux parents before crossing an SSH relay
and fails closed when a shared-client topology cannot be attributed safely.
.PP
Neovim keeps split and application-tab operations local, then delegates every
tmux boundary to this command so client and session provenance have one owner.
tmux bindings use
.B --parent
with exact client identity after their current scope declines.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B pane-select
Select left, down, up, or right. Pane navigation stops at the outermost tmux;
Termnav does not assume terminal-emulator panes have tmux semantics.
.TP
.B tab-select
Select the next or previous tab. A scope with one tab declines outward.
.TP
.B tab-move
Move the current tab left or right. A scope with multiple tabs owns the action,
including a no-op at its reorder boundary.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The request was handled or safely consumed.
.TP
.B 1
Routing failed or became ambiguous; no fallback should run.
.TP
.B 3
The requested scope declined. This result is primarily used by internal relay
adapters.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR termnav-relay (1),
.BR termnav-tmux-context (1)
